assName":"active","href":"/en/tip/29-04","data-status":"active"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["04"]},"People who lose a loved one to suicide, accident, or homicide should seek professional help rather than trying to cope alone"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-05"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["05"]},"In the first six months after losing a spouse, assign one trusted person to oversee meals, sleep, medication for chronic conditions, and follow‑up appointments"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-06"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["06"]},"For those without family or friends, replace “the person watching over you” with three simple things: a neighbor who can enter your home, a spot on the community outreach list, and emergency contacts saved on your phone"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-07"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["07"]},"After a parent dies, tell the child the truth, let him attend the funeral, and don’t send him to another environment"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-08"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["08"]},"Still stuck in grief after half a year, unable to move on — when to see a psychiatrist or clinical psychologist"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-09"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["09"]},"Don’t spend money on grief counseling right away — first check whether your grief is truly stuck (see the symptoms listed in item 8)"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-10"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["10"]},"Don’t drop yibao or turn to alcohol after separating or divorcing"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-11"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["11"]},"Call 12356 for general support, 12355 for minors and teens; for medical care, book a psychology clinic appointment"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-12"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["12"]},"In the first three months after a tragedy, postpone any irreversible major decisions"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/29-13"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["13"]},"Don’t treat death as a way to settle debts: life insurance won’t pay out for suicides within two years, workplace injuries won’t be recognized, and debts are still deducted from your estate first"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-tip-page"},"children":[{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-breadcrumb","aria-label":"Breadcrumb"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book"},"children":["Explore the book"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"aria-hidden":"true"},"children":["/"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book/29"},"children":["Chapter 29"," ·"," ","After experiencing a major setback"]}]},{"tag":"article","props":{"className":"life-entry-card status-unmarked is-standalone","id":"29-04"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-top"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-entry-number"},"children":["04"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-evidence grade-a"},"children":["Evidence"," ","A"]}]},{"tag":"h1","props":{"lang":"en"},"children":["People who lose a loved one to suicide, accident, or homicide should seek professional help rather than trying to cope alone"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"lang":"en","className":"life-entry-summary"},"children":["Within five years after losing a spouse to suicide, men are about 80% more likely to develop a mental disorder compared to the general population, while women are about 70% more likely. Compared to those whose spouses died from other causes, this risk is still 70% to 100% higher. Such bereaved individuals also tend to feel isolated and ashamed. This is precisely why they should actively seek help rather than waiting for things to get better on their own."]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-impact"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Calling 12356 is free of charge. Visiting a doctor and att…"]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["A nationwide Danish registry tracked 6.7 million adults from 1980 to 2014, totaling over 136 million person-ye…"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-actions","aria-label":"Mark: People who lose a loved one to suicide, accident, or homicide should seek professional help rather than trying to cope alone"},"children":[{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action done","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-check","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M20 6 9 17l-5-5"},"children":[]}]},"Done"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action todo","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-list-todo","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"rect","props":{"x":"3","y":"5","width":"6","height":"6","rx":"1"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m3 17 2 2 4-4"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 6h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 12h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 18h8"},"children":[]}]},"Plan to do"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action favorite","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-bookmark","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m19 21-7-4-7 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h10a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v16z"},"children":[]}]},"Save"]}," ",{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"social-share-trigger"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"5","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"6","cy":"12","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"19","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"8.59","x2":"15.42","y1":"13.51","y2":"17.49"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"15.41","x2":"8.59","y1":"6.51","y2":"10.49"},"children":[]}]},"Share this tip"]}]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-detail-toggle","aria-expanded":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"10","height":"10","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"currentColor","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"},"children":[]}]},"Hide details"]},{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-down rotated","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m6 9 6 6 6-6"},"children":[]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-details"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Calling 12356 is free of charge. Visiting a doctor and attending a psychological clinic costs the same as any other outpatient visit. The hard part is mustering the courage to reach out."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["A nationwide Danish registry tracked 6.7 million adults from 1980 to 2014, totaling over 136 million person-years of observation. For bereaved individuals whose spouses died by suicide, the relative risk of being newly diagnosed with a mental disorder within five years was as follows: for men, the IRR was 1.8 (95% CI 1.6–2.0), meaning a roughly 80% higher risk; for women, the IRR was 1.7 (1.6–1.8), representing a roughly 70% higher risk. Compared to those whose spouses died from other causes, the IRR for men was 1.7 (1.5–1.9) and for women 2.0 (1.9–2.2), again indicating a 70% to 100% higher risk. This group also showed higher rates of suicidal behavior, mortality, and need for municipal social assistance. Physical health risks such as cirrhosis and sleep disorders were also elevated. An additional 57 separate studies were reviewed without pooling their results. Bereavement due to suicide is linked to four key outcomes: a higher risk of suicide among surviving partners; a higher likelihood of parents being admitted to psychiatric care after their child’s suicide; a higher suicide risk among mothers after their adult child’s death; and a higher depression risk among children after their parents’ suicide. Compared to those grieving after violent deaths from other causes, people bereaved by suicide report feeling isolated and ashamed more often."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Original sources"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":["Erlangsen A, et al. (2017). Association Between Spousal Suicide and Mental, Physical, and Social Health Outcomes: A Longitudinal and Nationwide Register-Based Study. JAMA Psychiatry. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1001/jamapsychiatry.2017.0226","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.1001/jamapsychiatry.2017.0226"]},"；Pitman A, et al. (2014). Effects of suicide bereavement on mental health and suicide risk. The Lancet Psychiatry. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S2215-0366(14)70224-X","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.1016/S2215-0366(14)70224-X"]},"；Kristensen P 等 (2012). Bereavement and mental health after sudden and violent losses: a review. Psychiatry. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1521/psyc.2012.75.1.76","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.1521/psyc.2012.75.1.76"]},"（备注里那份综述）"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1001/jamapsychiatry.2017.0226","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"life-source-link"},"children":["Open source link"," ",{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"13","height":"13","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M15 3h6v6"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M10 14 21 3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"},"children":[]}]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Book note"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-content-reference"},"children":["Sudden, violent deaths refer to accidents, homicides, or disasters. After such events, rates of PTSD, depression, and prolonged grief are higher than after deaths from natural causes, and recovery tends to be slower. Guidance on handling suicidal thoughts is provided in Section 1, Item 25."]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-personal-note"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["My note"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button"},"children":["Write a reminder for yourself…"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager-link","href":"/en/tip/29-03"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-left","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M19 12H5"},"children":[]}]},{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"small","props":{},"children":["Previous"]},"After losing a job, it’s important to set a regular sleep schedule, keep yibao (basic medical insurance) active, and plan job searches methodically — don’t just stay at home all day"]}]},{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager-link next","href":"/en/tip/29-05"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"small","props":{},"children":["Next"]},"In the first six months after losing a spouse, assign one trusted person to oversee meals, sleep, medication for chronic conditions, and follow‑up appointments"]},{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-right","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path",